    {
      "id": "136",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 136,
        "body_ja": "",
        "body": "<p><span data-gp-id='109'>だけで</span> is a combination of the <span data-term='副助詞・ふくじょし'>adverbial particle</span> <span data-gp-id='43'>だけ</span>, and the <span data-term='格助詞・かくじょし'>case marking particle</span><span data-gp-id='36'>で</span>. This expression is regularly thought of as meaning 'just by (A), (B)'. However, the literal translation is a bit closer to 'with only (A), (B)'. This reflects the <span data-gp-id='36'>で</span> particle's standard usage of showing a 'tool' that is being used to achieve a certain result.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To use <span data-gp-id='109'>だけで</span>, simply attach it to the end of any (non ます) form of verb, or noun.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='180194'>\r\n<li data-study-question='180195'></ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='funfact'><h4>Fun Fact</h4>\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='43'>だけ</span> differs from <span data-gp-id='182'>しか</span> in one very important way. <span data-gp-id='43'>だけ</span> highlights that there is/was more than one option, but that only one thing was chosen/used. However, <span data-gp-id='182'>しか</span> implies that there is only one possible option to begin with.</p></section>"
      }
    },
